1
00:00:01,801 --> 00:00:05,605
MEGURO CHUO HOSPITAL

2
00:00:18,451 --> 00:00:19,419
Michiko...

3
00:00:27,327 --> 00:00:28,428
Dr. Daimon...

4
00:00:31,831 --> 00:00:32,699
Hiromi!

5
00:00:32,766 --> 00:00:33,666
Akira!

6
00:00:35,668 --> 00:00:36,636
Michiko...

7
00:00:36,703 --> 00:00:37,971
CT SCAN IN USE

8
00:00:55,522 --> 00:00:57,057
How did this happen?

9
00:00:57,924 --> 00:01:02,996
She's always been health conscious
and getting regular check-ups.

10
00:01:08,501 --> 00:01:10,003
I slept so well.

11
00:01:10,837 --> 00:01:11,938
Good morning.

12
00:01:12,005 --> 00:01:12,939
Good morning.

13
00:01:14,174 --> 00:01:16,443
How are you?
You should stay in bed.

14
00:01:16,576 --> 00:01:17,844
I'm fine.

15
00:01:20,246 --> 00:01:21,214
Let me see.

16
00:01:21,281 --> 00:01:22,148
See what?

17
00:01:26,753 --> 00:01:27,887
Turn around.

18
00:01:35,762 --> 00:01:37,864
Retroperitoneal sarcoma
stage 3.

19
00:01:38,331 --> 00:01:41,101
The tumor is wrapped around
the abdominal aorta.

20
00:01:41,367 --> 00:01:42,535
At this rate...

21
00:01:45,605 --> 00:01:47,774
I have three months at most.

22
00:01:48,541 --> 00:01:49,609
Dr. Daimon...

23
00:01:50,710 --> 00:01:51,811
Michiko...

24
00:01:53,580 --> 00:01:54,647
What a surprise, huh?

25
00:01:55,915 --> 00:01:58,618
Didn't you notice any symptoms?

26
00:01:58,685 --> 00:01:59,719
Not at all.

27
00:02:00,987 --> 00:02:02,155
A silent killer.

28
00:02:03,256 --> 00:02:06,126
Cancer that advances without
noticeable symptoms.

29
00:02:08,294 --> 00:02:09,529
It's incurable in Japan.

30
00:02:10,029 --> 00:02:12,031
I'll find a doctor overseas.

31
00:02:12,565 --> 00:02:15,368
I'll ask a friend in the U.S.

32
00:02:16,436 --> 00:02:18,138
I can cut it.

33
00:02:23,009 --> 00:02:26,546
<i>This is the story of</i>
<i>a lone wolf woman doctor.</i>

34
00:02:28,414 --> 00:02:29,883
<i>In 2017</i>

35
00:02:30,250 --> 00:02:35,221
<i>the university medical system</i>
<i>regained its once-lost authority</i>

36
00:02:35,688 --> 00:02:41,728
<i>and the system on which lives depend</i>
<i>strayed away from what it should be.</i>

37
00:02:41,895 --> 00:02:43,496
Esophagus cancer stage 4A.

38
00:02:43,830 --> 00:02:45,632
It's quite serious.

39
00:02:45,965 --> 00:02:48,601
Possibly invading the descending aorta.

40
00:02:48,735 --> 00:02:52,672
Surgical removal of the tumor
is extremely difficult.

41
00:02:52,805 --> 00:02:53,806
Can you do it?

42
00:02:55,508 --> 00:02:57,110
This operation?

43
00:02:58,811 --> 00:03:00,547
The only surgeon with the skill

44
00:03:01,381 --> 00:03:02,482
is Michiko Daimon.

45
00:03:02,682 --> 00:03:04,150
I agree.

46
00:03:04,350 --> 00:03:08,288
But we terminated the contract
with the locum doctor agency.

47
00:03:08,988 --> 00:03:13,993
And the patient is refusing to be
operated on by Daimon.

48
00:03:14,260 --> 00:03:15,428
Refusing?

49
00:03:15,929 --> 00:03:18,364
This patient knows Daimon?

50
00:03:19,265 --> 00:03:20,433
Who is it?

51
00:03:20,567 --> 00:03:21,534
This patient.

52
00:03:25,738 --> 00:03:28,775
I'm the chairman of
the Japan Doctors Club.

53
00:03:30,176 --> 00:03:32,178
Even if I have cancer

54
00:03:33,012 --> 00:03:35,215
I won't have a freelancer operate on me.

55
00:03:40,753 --> 00:03:42,222
I want

56
00:03:44,424 --> 00:03:46,793
Totei surgeons to save my life.

57
00:03:48,394 --> 00:03:49,295
Us?

58
00:03:50,029 --> 00:03:52,165
- Chairman Uchikanda's...
- Operation?

59
00:03:52,332 --> 00:03:54,067
If this operation fails

60
00:03:54,267 --> 00:03:57,770
it's essentially the end of
your medical careers.

61
00:03:58,404 --> 00:03:59,973
- Yes sir.
- However...

62
00:04:01,007 --> 00:04:04,911
there's a brave doctor,
a Totei University graduate,

63
00:04:05,745 --> 00:04:10,850
who volunteered to perform
this high-risk operation.

64
00:04:11,417 --> 00:04:12,685
A Totei graduate?

65
00:04:12,752 --> 00:04:14,387
Show him in.

66
00:04:17,423 --> 00:04:18,291
Come in.

67
00:04:21,594 --> 00:04:22,695
Hello, gentlemen.

68
00:04:24,864 --> 00:04:26,699
It's been a while.

69
00:04:26,933 --> 00:04:28,234
Dr. Kaji.

70
00:04:31,170 --> 00:04:35,541
I believe he needs no introduction.

71
00:04:35,675 --> 00:04:38,845
The wizard of laparoscopy,
Dr. Takashi Kaji.

72
00:04:38,978 --> 00:04:41,214
- It's Hideki Kaji.
- Is that right?

73
00:04:41,381 --> 00:04:42,649
I have shocking news.

74
00:04:45,585 --> 00:04:49,355
Chairman Uchikanda has cancer.

75
00:04:49,922 --> 00:04:54,761
<i>In the midst of this, doctors free</i>
<i>from any establishment emerged</i>.

76
00:04:55,395 --> 00:04:59,966
<i>Freelance doctors, in other words,</i>
<i>lone wolf doctors.</i>

77
00:05:00,099 --> 00:05:01,934
Esophagus cancer stage 4A.

78
00:05:02,201 --> 00:05:03,503
A successful surgery will

79
00:05:03,569 --> 00:05:06,439
make me Totei's chief surgeon.

80
00:05:06,506 --> 00:05:09,108
Those three doctors will
be reporting to me.

81
00:05:09,242 --> 00:05:13,579
Is that why you agreed to do the surgery?

82
00:05:13,780 --> 00:05:16,249
A surgery too frightening to accept.

83
00:05:16,349 --> 00:05:19,152
One must gamble to advance his career.

84
00:05:19,285 --> 00:05:20,887
Your turn, Ben Casey.

85
00:05:22,221 --> 00:05:24,857
Ben Casey, this one?

86
00:05:24,991 --> 00:05:25,925
Okay.

87
00:05:26,926 --> 00:05:29,362
This surgery's too difficult for you.

88
00:05:29,495 --> 00:05:32,665
I know. That's why I'm here.

89
00:05:33,032 --> 00:05:34,300
What do you mean?

90
00:05:35,535 --> 00:05:37,437
Will you help me?

91
00:05:38,638 --> 00:05:40,907
The two of us can't go wrong.

92
00:05:41,040 --> 00:05:42,508
It won't be a gamble.

93
00:05:45,945 --> 00:05:47,714
Next. This one?

94
00:05:48,481 --> 00:05:49,449
Okay?

95
00:05:50,350 --> 00:05:53,252
Naturally, when I become the chief surgeon

96
00:05:53,386 --> 00:05:55,855
I'll reinstate your contract
with Totei.

97
00:05:56,923 --> 00:05:58,191
I decline.

98
00:05:58,491 --> 00:05:59,792
Why?

99
00:06:00,093 --> 00:06:04,197
Are you scared because the patient
is Chairman Uchikanda?

100
00:06:04,297 --> 00:06:06,899
I'm going to Boston.

101
00:06:07,433 --> 00:06:09,869
A hospital there is waiting for you.

102
00:06:09,936 --> 00:06:10,970
Sorry.

103
00:06:11,137 --> 00:06:13,272
Are you serious?
You have a job there?

104
00:06:13,639 --> 00:06:15,174
Is it that lucrative?

105
00:06:15,675 --> 00:06:16,909
Ron!

106
00:06:16,976 --> 00:06:19,278
A nice "mangan" hand.

107
00:06:19,345 --> 00:06:21,347
Yay!

108
00:06:21,414 --> 00:06:24,650
I'll let you have a big win anytime.

109
00:06:24,717 --> 00:06:27,053
So help me.
We're friends, aren't we?

110
00:06:27,420 --> 00:06:29,389
- I decline.
- Please, Demon.

111
00:06:29,455 --> 00:06:30,790
Don't decline.

112
00:06:30,890 --> 00:06:32,658
Do a favor for a friend.

113
00:06:32,759 --> 00:06:35,328
- Don't yell at me.
- Hey!

114
00:06:35,762 --> 00:06:36,763
I'm so sorry.

115
00:06:37,497 --> 00:06:39,432
After much deliberation

116
00:06:39,932 --> 00:06:44,370
I've decided not to accept
Chairman Uchikanda's operation.

117
00:06:44,871 --> 00:06:46,205
What happened?

118
00:06:46,439 --> 00:06:48,541
Did Daimon say no?

119
00:06:48,741 --> 00:06:50,143
She did. I mean...

120
00:06:50,243 --> 00:06:54,080
Who is this Daimon person?
I don't know any freelancers.

121
00:06:54,514 --> 00:06:55,748
He asked her.

122
00:06:55,848 --> 00:06:57,016
He definitely asked her.

123
00:06:57,450 --> 00:06:58,651
I was hoping

124
00:06:58,818 --> 00:07:01,921
you'd be able to talk her into

125
00:07:02,288 --> 00:07:06,459
being the surgeon's double
for the operation.

126
00:07:07,493 --> 00:07:10,196
We'll have to come up
with a different plan.

127
00:07:10,863 --> 00:07:12,298
A different plan?

128
00:07:14,033 --> 00:07:16,269
- Dr. Nishiyama, are you here?
- Yes.

129
00:07:17,370 --> 00:07:18,404
Excuse me.

130
00:07:19,772 --> 00:07:20,606
Who's this kid?

131
00:07:25,812 --> 00:07:26,813
Dr. Nishiyama...

132
00:07:28,147 --> 00:07:32,318
I want you to operate on
Chairman Uchikanda.

133
00:07:33,553 --> 00:07:34,487
But...

134
00:07:34,587 --> 00:07:35,488
Why him?

135
00:07:35,855 --> 00:07:36,856
So who is he?

136
00:07:36,923 --> 00:07:39,692
Dr. Nishiyama is Chairman Uchikanda's...

137
00:07:41,994 --> 00:07:42,829
son.

138
00:07:43,996 --> 00:07:44,864
His son?

139
00:07:44,931 --> 00:07:45,832
Are you serious?

140
00:07:45,965 --> 00:07:50,403
A young surgeon takes on
a challenging operation

141
00:07:51,304 --> 00:07:53,372
to save his father.

142
00:07:54,040 --> 00:07:54,941
What do you think?

143
00:07:56,409 --> 00:07:57,510
I see.

144
00:07:58,578 --> 00:08:00,913
It'd be a moving tale.

145
00:08:02,548 --> 00:08:03,382
I decline.

146
00:08:03,516 --> 00:08:04,650
You decline?

147
00:08:05,117 --> 00:08:09,555
No. This operation is
too difficult for me.

148
00:08:10,223 --> 00:08:11,424
There's no one else.

149
00:08:13,659 --> 00:08:14,894
Who can do it.

150
00:08:18,931 --> 00:08:20,132
Don't kill the patient.

151
00:08:20,199 --> 00:08:21,200
Daimon.

152
00:08:21,601 --> 00:08:22,802
You're banned.

153
00:08:23,936 --> 00:08:25,538
Only I can do this.

154
00:08:25,805 --> 00:08:28,975
Only you?
But you said you won't.

155
00:08:31,878 --> 00:08:34,146
Retroperitoneal sarcoma
stage 3.

156
00:08:35,147 --> 00:08:36,048
What?

157
00:08:37,083 --> 00:08:39,619
He has esophagus cancer
stage 4A.

158
00:08:40,152 --> 00:08:41,754
The patient with retroperitoneal sarcoma

159
00:08:42,421 --> 00:08:43,556
is me.

160
00:08:45,858 --> 00:08:47,226
You?

161
00:08:48,227 --> 00:08:49,328
Wait...

162
00:08:50,129 --> 00:08:52,164
You have retroperitoneal sarcoma?

163
00:08:53,132 --> 00:08:56,035
A 13-cm tumor around the abdominal aorta.

164
00:08:58,104 --> 00:09:01,040
Is that why you turned
down this surgery?

165
00:09:01,207 --> 00:09:03,309
I can't operate in my condition.

166
00:09:06,679 --> 00:09:07,647
But...

167
00:09:08,281 --> 00:09:11,017
if I take opioids to alleviate the pain

168
00:09:12,018 --> 00:09:12,952
I can do it.

169
00:09:15,087 --> 00:09:16,389
Will you, Daimon?

170
00:09:17,356 --> 00:09:18,624
Operate on the chairman?

171
00:09:19,759 --> 00:09:20,593
Yes.

172
00:09:21,427 --> 00:09:22,929
In your condition?!

173
00:09:23,029 --> 00:09:24,297
Good for you.

174
00:09:24,997 --> 00:09:26,098
I applaud you.

175
00:09:28,434 --> 00:09:31,437
I'll lift your ban from
Totei University Hospital

176
00:09:32,204 --> 00:09:33,673
just for this surgery.

177
00:09:34,740 --> 00:09:36,042
I welcome you back.

178
00:09:36,475 --> 00:09:38,210
<i>This woman, for example.</i>

179
00:09:38,911 --> 00:09:42,982
<i>Despising the herd mentality, authority</i>
<i>and institutional restraints...</i>

180
00:09:43,549 --> 00:09:49,522
<i>Her solo weapons are her license</i>
<i>and the skills she has acquired.</i>

181
00:09:51,090 --> 00:09:53,659
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

182
00:09:54,160 --> 00:09:57,396
<i>Also known as Doctor-X.</i>

183
00:10:26,525 --> 00:10:29,395
Is it true that Dr. Daimon
has retroperitoneal sarcoma?

184
00:10:30,630 --> 00:10:31,998
She's not getting treatment?

185
00:10:32,832 --> 00:10:35,267
You know she won't listen to anybody.

186
00:10:37,269 --> 00:10:41,941
We'll start a closed-door conference
for Chairman Uchikanda's operation.

187
00:10:43,376 --> 00:10:45,811
The diagnosis is esophagus
cancer stage 4A.

188
00:10:46,112 --> 00:10:49,181
A 7-cm tumor in the midthoracic esophagus.

189
00:10:49,615 --> 00:10:51,751
Possible invasion into
the descending aorta.

190
00:10:52,251 --> 00:10:55,688
Subtotal esophagectomy and
posterior mediastinal reconstruction.

191
00:10:56,989 --> 00:10:59,358
It'll take 2.5 hours to remove the tumor.

192
00:10:59,925 --> 00:11:01,627
1.5 hours to reconstruct
the digestive tract.

193
00:11:02,161 --> 00:11:05,698
We'll try to finish in four hours.

194
00:11:06,399 --> 00:11:08,934
Four hours? That's impossible.

195
00:11:09,101 --> 00:11:10,870
What if it takes longer?

196
00:11:12,171 --> 00:11:13,439
I'm sorry.

197
00:11:13,906 --> 00:11:17,443
We'll also need a hybrid
vascular graft.

198
00:11:17,576 --> 00:11:19,045
Hybrid vascular graft?

199
00:11:19,612 --> 00:11:22,381
The latest vascular prosthesis
developed in the US.

200
00:11:22,948 --> 00:11:24,750
It's not available here yet.

201
00:11:26,385 --> 00:11:27,353
Fine.

202
00:11:28,354 --> 00:11:31,657
Director Hiruma said money is no object.

203
00:11:32,692 --> 00:11:35,027
Buy anything you need.

204
00:11:35,695 --> 00:11:36,595
Yes sir.

205
00:11:37,730 --> 00:11:40,032
It's noon. I'm going to lunch.

206
00:11:45,638 --> 00:11:47,740
Is she really sick?

207
00:12:12,965 --> 00:12:15,334
This is Daimon's test results.

208
00:12:15,568 --> 00:12:19,071
The tumor is wrapped around
the abdominal aorta.

209
00:12:19,638 --> 00:12:23,275
It's also spread to the superior
mesenteric and celiac arteries.

210
00:12:25,277 --> 00:12:26,979
- Daimon...
- Director Hiruma.

211
00:12:27,513 --> 00:12:32,118
I think you should reconsider having
her operate on the chairman.

212
00:12:33,552 --> 00:12:34,787
Reconsider?

213
00:12:36,522 --> 00:12:39,024
If she operates in her condition

214
00:12:40,292 --> 00:12:41,961
and if something happens...

215
00:12:42,294 --> 00:12:43,496
If something happens?

216
00:12:45,731 --> 00:12:48,868
Dr. Torii...

217
00:12:49,935 --> 00:12:54,707
I heard Daimon saved your life.

218
00:12:55,908 --> 00:12:57,009
That's right.

219
00:12:57,977 --> 00:12:58,911
You see...

220
00:12:59,645 --> 00:13:03,783
She saved my life too.

221
00:13:06,051 --> 00:13:09,121
That's because Daimon

222
00:13:09,955 --> 00:13:11,157
as a surgeon

223
00:13:12,291 --> 00:13:14,326
did her job impeccably.

224
00:13:17,930 --> 00:13:19,899
This operation on Chairman Uchikanda

225
00:13:21,467 --> 00:13:25,070
must also be performed impeccably.

226
00:13:29,108 --> 00:13:31,243
If she takes opioids

227
00:13:32,912 --> 00:13:35,981
she said she could
operate on the chairman.

228
00:13:36,882 --> 00:13:42,688
Even if the pain is temporarily eased,
she'll be risking her life...

229
00:13:42,755 --> 00:13:44,356
Don't worry about it.

230
00:13:46,292 --> 00:13:48,394
She can handle it.

231
00:13:49,228 --> 00:13:50,930
She doesn't fail.

232
00:13:53,132 --> 00:13:55,701
But if something happens to her

233
00:13:56,268 --> 00:13:57,670
the chairman's life would...

234
00:13:57,736 --> 00:13:59,338
Then Dr. Torii...

235
00:14:00,372 --> 00:14:02,041
Will you operate on him?

236
00:14:16,155 --> 00:14:18,157
Chairman Uchikanda's operation

237
00:14:19,325 --> 00:14:21,694
will be performed by Michiko Daimon.

238
00:14:22,528 --> 00:14:23,395
Is that clear?

239
00:14:26,665 --> 00:14:27,800
No "yes sir"?

240
00:14:31,237 --> 00:14:33,072
I don't hear a "yes sir."

241
00:14:33,505 --> 00:14:34,740
Yes sir.

242
00:14:35,941 --> 00:14:39,078
Everybody here at Totei
will work together

243
00:14:39,879 --> 00:14:42,815
to make your operation a success.

244
00:14:43,883 --> 00:14:44,717
Right?

245
00:14:44,984 --> 00:14:45,951
Yes sir.

246
00:14:46,318 --> 00:14:48,220
Who will be operating on me?

247
00:14:48,420 --> 00:14:52,958
The lead surgeon will be
Dr. Nishiyama.

248
00:14:55,494 --> 00:14:59,798
Nothing is stronger than
a son's love for his father.

249
00:15:00,065 --> 00:15:04,503
Please understand how he feels.

250
00:15:06,272 --> 00:15:08,507
I'd like to be alone with him.

251
00:15:09,408 --> 00:15:10,376
Sure.

252
00:15:25,190 --> 00:15:28,227
I'm happy you're operating on me.

253
00:15:31,430 --> 00:15:32,398
I'm proud of you.

254
00:15:38,537 --> 00:15:39,405
You're lying.

255
00:15:43,609 --> 00:15:44,510
You're lying.

256
00:15:46,345 --> 00:15:51,183
You want a doctor like Dr. Daimon
who never fails.

257
00:15:52,518 --> 00:15:56,855
Isn't that what you want,
now that you're a patient?

258
00:16:01,026 --> 00:16:01,961
But...

259
00:16:03,429 --> 00:16:06,298
your position won't allow it.

260
00:16:08,934 --> 00:16:10,970
If a freelancer operates on you

261
00:16:12,504 --> 00:16:14,373
university hospitals will lose authority.

262
00:16:16,942 --> 00:16:17,876
You're going to

263
00:16:19,845 --> 00:16:24,650
get killed by the institution
you built yourself.

264
00:16:28,320 --> 00:16:31,523
Stop talking nonsense and
prepare for the operation.

265
00:16:33,559 --> 00:16:34,393
Leave.

266
00:16:39,565 --> 00:16:40,666
I said leave.

267
00:17:21,006 --> 00:17:24,576
She won't stop staring at
the chairman's data.

268
00:17:25,477 --> 00:17:28,714
She's been on her feet
for about an hour.

269
00:17:43,095 --> 00:17:44,063
Daimon.

270
00:17:44,463 --> 00:17:48,434
Stop worrying about the chairman
and start worrying about yourself.

271
00:17:51,170 --> 00:17:52,037
What?

272
00:17:53,906 --> 00:17:55,007
Daimon.

273
00:17:55,274 --> 00:17:56,909
It's five o'clock.
We're going home.

274
00:17:57,509 --> 00:17:58,477
Oh, that.

275
00:17:58,911 --> 00:18:00,746
Take care of Daimon.

276
00:18:22,868 --> 00:18:23,769
Dr. Daimon.

277
00:18:25,471 --> 00:18:26,538
That man is

278
00:18:27,005 --> 00:18:31,176
the one trying to expel freelancers
from university hospitals.

279
00:18:31,743 --> 00:18:36,048
Why are you pushing yourself
so hard to save him?

280
00:18:37,316 --> 00:18:40,853
You should start getting
treatment yourself.

281
00:18:41,120 --> 00:18:42,688
He's your father, right?

282
00:18:43,689 --> 00:18:44,957
You want him to stay alive.

283
00:18:47,326 --> 00:18:49,495
An enemy or an ally.

284
00:18:50,062 --> 00:18:52,664
A good guy or a bad guy.

285
00:18:53,265 --> 00:18:55,100
It doesn't matter to her.

286
00:18:56,401 --> 00:18:59,138
She operates on patients
to save their lives.

287
00:19:00,239 --> 00:19:01,673
Regardless of who they are.

288
00:19:03,475 --> 00:19:04,710
Michiko Daimon is...

289
00:19:07,412 --> 00:19:08,780
that kind of doctor.

290
00:19:16,822 --> 00:19:18,457
KOREAN BBQ DISCOUNT TICKET

291
00:19:22,394 --> 00:19:26,231
What do you think Daimon's life
is all about?

292
00:19:27,633 --> 00:19:28,867
Was she happy?

293
00:19:29,201 --> 00:19:31,603
Special skills, surgery.
Hobby, surgery.

294
00:19:32,104 --> 00:19:34,907
She's been constantly
operating on patients.

295
00:19:35,307 --> 00:19:37,776
She must have been happy in her own way.

296
00:19:38,443 --> 00:19:39,811
You think so?

297
00:19:41,079 --> 00:19:43,282
I can't help feeling sorry for her.

298
00:19:43,482 --> 00:19:44,483
Why?

299
00:19:45,951 --> 00:19:49,855
She's cured every patient with
all kinds of diseases

300
00:19:51,223 --> 00:19:52,891
but now that she herself is sick

301
00:19:54,059 --> 00:19:55,861
there's no one to cure her.

302
00:19:58,397 --> 00:20:00,365
What could be more tragic?

303
00:20:00,432 --> 00:20:01,833
Nothing.

304
00:20:03,869 --> 00:20:04,736
All right.

305
00:20:05,504 --> 00:20:06,939
I'll cut it out.

306
00:20:08,307 --> 00:20:09,608
I'll operate on Demon.

307
00:20:10,342 --> 00:20:11,243
Good for you.

308
00:20:11,877 --> 00:20:13,478
I applaud you, Dr. Kaji.

309
00:20:13,545 --> 00:20:16,048
I, Takashi Ebina, will join you.

310
00:20:16,114 --> 00:20:17,683
Mamoru Hara will too.

311
00:20:17,816 --> 00:20:19,818
As will Hikaru Morimoto.

312
00:20:19,885 --> 00:20:21,620
Okay then.

313
00:20:22,354 --> 00:20:25,424
We'll each cut a little bit.

314
00:20:25,524 --> 00:20:29,027
No. It's not a sumo wrestler's
hair-cutting ceremony.

315
00:20:29,628 --> 00:20:31,897
"Dosukoi"!
Sumo wrestlers' battle cry.

316
00:20:32,497 --> 00:20:34,733
Dosukoi! Dosukoi!

317
00:20:34,800 --> 00:20:37,536
Go, Daimon! Dosukoi!

318
00:20:37,603 --> 00:20:40,572
We'll cut out her tumor!

319
00:20:40,939 --> 00:20:42,174
Shove it out!

320
00:20:42,241 --> 00:20:44,843
Yeah! Dosukoi!

321
00:20:45,043 --> 00:20:46,612
Dosukoi! Dosukoi!

322
00:20:47,045 --> 00:20:50,048
NON-ALCOHOLIC BEER

323
00:20:50,215 --> 00:20:51,617
- Here you go.
- Thanks.

324
00:20:54,253 --> 00:20:55,454
I got them.

325
00:20:55,520 --> 00:20:56,655
- Thanks.
- Which one?

326
00:20:56,722 --> 00:20:57,589
This one.

327
00:20:57,656 --> 00:20:59,524
- Are you sure?
- Yeah.

328
00:21:02,194 --> 00:21:04,363
- How are you feeling?
- Fine.

329
00:21:09,167 --> 00:21:11,103
So hot and yummy.

330
00:21:14,273 --> 00:21:15,173
What are you doing?

331
00:21:15,274 --> 00:21:17,109
I can't eat hot things.

332
00:21:17,209 --> 00:21:20,212
Really? I didn't know.

333
00:21:20,279 --> 00:21:22,347
I never told you?

334
00:21:22,514 --> 00:21:24,383
- Lame.
- Shut up.

335
00:21:31,823 --> 00:21:33,558
Dr. Daimon.

336
00:21:35,460 --> 00:21:37,229
Why are you so strong?

337
00:21:40,465 --> 00:21:43,201
I was so frantic.

338
00:21:52,110 --> 00:21:55,714
I never thought about it
before this happened.

339
00:21:56,581 --> 00:21:57,616
About what?

340
00:22:02,187 --> 00:22:03,221
Every doctor should

341
00:22:04,856 --> 00:22:06,758
experience being a patient.

342
00:22:08,427 --> 00:22:09,328
What?

343
00:22:11,697 --> 00:22:12,864
Surprisingly it's...

344
00:22:15,667 --> 00:22:16,802
scary being a patient.

345
00:22:19,971 --> 00:22:21,039
I didn't know.

346
00:22:26,745 --> 00:22:27,913
Dr. Daimon...

347
00:22:34,152 --> 00:22:37,622
When I got sick,
you asked me if there was

348
00:22:38,423 --> 00:22:40,726
something I wanted to do.

349
00:22:40,892 --> 00:22:41,760
I remember that.

350
00:22:41,827 --> 00:22:43,462
What about you?

351
00:22:43,528 --> 00:22:45,530
Let me think.

352
00:22:45,597 --> 00:22:49,434
If it's something we can do
together, let's do it now.

353
00:22:49,501 --> 00:22:51,937
- Bath house, mahjong...
- Those things?

354
00:22:53,305 --> 00:22:54,172
Yeah.

355
00:22:57,209 --> 00:22:58,710
Let's see...

356
00:23:04,516 --> 00:23:06,651
I can't think of anything.

357
00:23:08,653 --> 00:23:10,856
Really? Nothing?

358
00:23:10,956 --> 00:23:11,857
Because...

359
00:23:13,091 --> 00:23:14,659
I'm not planning to die.

360
00:23:20,031 --> 00:23:24,403
No matter how difficult
the operation, I've never

361
00:23:27,005 --> 00:23:28,607
backed out on a patient.

362
00:23:35,647 --> 00:23:36,848
I still won't.

363
00:23:41,086 --> 00:23:45,424
Even if I'm the patient myself.

364
00:24:07,078 --> 00:24:08,280
It's about time.

365
00:24:09,314 --> 00:24:10,248
That.

366
00:24:11,283 --> 00:24:12,284
It cooled down.

367
00:24:13,685 --> 00:24:16,288
Just the right temperature for you.

368
00:24:16,488 --> 00:24:17,322
Yeah?

369
00:24:17,622 --> 00:24:19,391
Not hot at all.

370
00:24:19,491 --> 00:24:21,426
It's perfect.

371
00:24:23,595 --> 00:24:24,596
Don't laugh.

372
00:25:11,176 --> 00:25:13,745
I'm home. Cold...

373
00:25:22,888 --> 00:25:23,922
Michiko.

374
00:25:25,390 --> 00:25:26,658
What's the matter?

375
00:25:28,326 --> 00:25:32,364
Wow... You drank so much.

376
00:25:33,164 --> 00:25:35,000
Let's go to Boston right now.

377
00:25:36,201 --> 00:25:40,672
Brilliant doctors are ready
to operate on you.

378
00:25:41,273 --> 00:25:42,774
They're waiting.

379
00:25:43,608 --> 00:25:46,978
I can't. I have to operate tomorrow.

380
00:25:47,612 --> 00:25:50,549
Yours is the day after tomorrow.

381
00:25:51,349 --> 00:25:55,987
They had to squeeze you in.
It's the only day they have.

382
00:25:56,555 --> 00:25:58,757
If you operate tomorrow,
it'll be too late.

383
00:26:00,392 --> 00:26:04,062
Only I can do tomorrow's operation.
You know that.

384
00:26:08,967 --> 00:26:12,437
You'd do anything for the patient but

385
00:26:13,605 --> 00:26:17,008
why do you put yourself
on the back burner?

386
00:26:18,310 --> 00:26:20,512
You're a patient too, Michiko!

387
00:26:28,687 --> 00:26:33,525
If you won't go, I'll operate on you.

388
00:26:37,495 --> 00:26:39,497
Akira...

389
00:26:42,267 --> 00:26:43,501
I know.

390
00:26:45,270 --> 00:26:47,606
I know I can't anymore.

391
00:26:49,040 --> 00:26:52,944
I haven't held a scalpel for years now.

392
00:26:57,716 --> 00:26:58,683
It's frustrating.

393
00:27:00,885 --> 00:27:01,920
So frustrating.

394
00:27:04,389 --> 00:27:05,924
I can't operate on

395
00:27:07,859 --> 00:27:11,997
my most beloved pupil at
the most critical time of her life.

396
00:27:13,765 --> 00:27:17,469
Why...? Why did I even

397
00:27:18,336 --> 00:27:20,305
become a doctor?

398
00:27:25,944 --> 00:27:31,683
I want you to stay alive
for much, much longer.

399
00:27:33,818 --> 00:27:35,120
You have to.

400
00:27:37,789 --> 00:27:38,990
So Michiko...

401
00:27:39,824 --> 00:27:43,328
Please do as I say.

402
00:27:44,095 --> 00:27:44,996
Michiko...

403
00:27:46,264 --> 00:27:47,599
Go to Boston.

404
00:27:48,566 --> 00:27:51,236
Please... I beg you.

405
00:27:51,736 --> 00:27:53,838
Michiko, please!

406
00:28:11,222 --> 00:28:12,891
Okay, Akira.

407
00:28:18,063 --> 00:28:21,332
I understand, so stop crying.

408
00:28:23,768 --> 00:28:25,236
Michiko...

409
00:28:25,537 --> 00:28:27,238
You're being silly.

410
00:28:29,107 --> 00:28:30,675
You silly man.

411
00:29:51,890 --> 00:29:53,158
I'm going.

412
00:30:15,680 --> 00:30:16,915
You're in stable condition.

413
00:30:17,549 --> 00:30:19,384
Good luck with your surgery.

414
00:30:19,450 --> 00:30:20,552
Thank you.

415
00:30:26,691 --> 00:30:27,692
Excuse me.

416
00:30:30,495 --> 00:30:32,597
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

417
00:30:39,237 --> 00:30:40,705
I'll do my best.

418
00:30:44,275 --> 00:30:45,543
Please wish me luck.

419
00:30:49,414 --> 00:30:50,415
I'm counting on you.

420
00:30:54,652 --> 00:30:55,587
Naoyuki...

421
00:31:29,020 --> 00:31:30,355
It hurts...

422
00:32:00,251 --> 00:32:02,086
Dr. Daimon is late.

423
00:32:02,186 --> 00:32:03,054
Did you call her?

424
00:32:03,154 --> 00:32:05,256
Many times. She won't answer.

425
00:32:05,456 --> 00:32:07,926
Where the hell is she?

426
00:32:18,403 --> 00:32:19,771
Daimon isn't here yet.

427
00:32:19,904 --> 00:32:22,006
Maybe she got cold feet.

428
00:32:23,942 --> 00:32:25,877
Did something happen to her?

429
00:32:26,744 --> 00:32:27,745
All set?

430
00:32:31,082 --> 00:32:32,216
Dr. Daimon...

431
00:32:47,332 --> 00:32:49,534
The operation hasn't started yet?

432
00:32:51,736 --> 00:32:53,905
Read between the lines.

433
00:32:54,038 --> 00:32:56,808
Please read between the lines.

434
00:32:57,041 --> 00:32:58,409
Right.

435
00:33:09,320 --> 00:33:11,322
Is everything in order?

436
00:33:13,658 --> 00:33:15,193
Start the operation.

437
00:33:15,360 --> 00:33:17,061
Yes, Director.

438
00:33:20,498 --> 00:33:23,601
Director Hiruma wants us
to start the operation.

439
00:33:23,701 --> 00:33:24,635
What?

440
00:33:26,037 --> 00:33:28,106
What should we do?

441
00:33:29,574 --> 00:33:31,843
The lead surgeon isn't here.

442
00:33:36,114 --> 00:33:37,482
I'll do it.

443
00:33:41,319 --> 00:33:42,186
Dr. Nishiyama...

444
00:33:45,456 --> 00:33:46,724
He's my father.

445
00:33:48,092 --> 00:33:49,093
I'll assist you.

446
00:33:52,897 --> 00:33:57,969
Subtotal esophagectomy and
posterior mediastinal reconstruction.

447
00:33:58,436 --> 00:33:59,570
Let's begin.

448
00:33:59,804 --> 00:34:01,072
Yes, Doctor.

449
00:34:01,272 --> 00:34:05,443
Vitals. BP 124 over 82.
Pulse 85, normal sinus rhythm.

450
00:34:05,777 --> 00:34:06,844
Scalpel.

451
00:34:22,593 --> 00:34:23,795
Monopolar.

452
00:34:28,366 --> 00:34:31,035
Can they really do it without Daimon?

453
00:34:32,270 --> 00:34:35,640
Does Director Hiruma think
it's okay if they fail?

454
00:34:36,274 --> 00:34:41,546
A son takes on a challenging
operation to save his father

455
00:34:42,447 --> 00:34:44,348
but regrettably fails.

456
00:34:46,150 --> 00:34:49,187
Nothing could be more moving than that.

457
00:34:51,322 --> 00:34:53,524
I'm glad I'm not there.

458
00:35:08,406 --> 00:35:09,240
You're fast.

459
00:35:09,407 --> 00:35:11,943
You've improved your skills.

460
00:35:18,049 --> 00:35:19,016
Uh-oh...

461
00:35:22,987 --> 00:35:24,989
Rigid adhesion to the aortic wall.

462
00:35:26,424 --> 00:35:29,427
And extensive invasion into
the descending aorta.

463
00:35:30,661 --> 00:35:32,363
I want to check in more detail.

464
00:35:32,430 --> 00:35:34,899
Please expand the operative field.

465
00:35:36,000 --> 00:35:37,368
That's not possible.

466
00:35:42,540 --> 00:35:43,374
Nishiyama!

467
00:35:43,908 --> 00:35:45,543
It's too dangerous to keep going.

468
00:35:45,710 --> 00:35:46,711
Stop the operation.

469
00:35:47,011 --> 00:35:49,313
Dr. Nishiyama, don't kill your father.

470
00:35:50,681 --> 00:35:51,516
Don't kill him!

471
00:35:52,083 --> 00:35:53,184
He's your father!

472
00:36:23,181 --> 00:36:24,215
Inoperable.

473
00:36:29,954 --> 00:36:31,222
Leave it open.

474
00:36:31,289 --> 00:36:32,223
Dr. Daimon...

475
00:36:33,858 --> 00:36:35,526
You're late, Demon.

476
00:36:36,928 --> 00:36:39,697
There she is! Dr. Daimon!

477
00:36:40,097 --> 00:36:41,599
Yes, she's here.

478
00:36:47,905 --> 00:36:48,839
Daimon...

479
00:36:52,977 --> 00:36:53,844
You did good.

480
00:36:54,779 --> 00:36:56,113
Dr. Daimon...

481
00:36:57,014 --> 00:36:58,649
Combined aortic resection.

482
00:36:58,749 --> 00:37:00,284
- Change.
- Yes, Doctor.

483
00:37:05,189 --> 00:37:06,324
Metzen.

484
00:37:40,825 --> 00:37:43,694
Michiko... Don't die...

485
00:37:44,362 --> 00:37:46,397
Michiko... Michiko!

486
00:37:54,972 --> 00:37:56,073
Michiko?

487
00:38:17,361 --> 00:38:18,329
This is...

488
00:38:32,376 --> 00:38:34,378
Patch closure completed
on descending aorta.

489
00:38:34,478 --> 00:38:35,313
Raise the loupe.

490
00:38:35,379 --> 00:38:36,881
Yes, Doctor.

491
00:38:37,948 --> 00:38:40,551
- Vitals?
- BP 117 over 75.

492
00:38:40,618 --> 00:38:43,154
- Pulse 78, normal sinus rhythm.
- Okay.

493
00:38:43,421 --> 00:38:44,855
Abdominal incision after hemostasis.

494
00:38:44,922 --> 00:38:45,956
Bipolar.

495
00:38:52,029 --> 00:38:55,833
I'm awestruck by your skills
as usual, Demon.

496
00:38:56,300 --> 00:38:58,235
Stop babbling and move your hands.

497
00:38:58,302 --> 00:39:01,739
- I missed hearing that.
- Okay.

498
00:39:15,319 --> 00:39:16,721
One hurdle cleared.

499
00:39:17,588 --> 00:39:20,024
How many times have I said this?

500
00:39:20,458 --> 00:39:21,659
Daimon is amazing.

501
00:39:24,762 --> 00:39:25,930
Excuse me.

502
00:39:28,032 --> 00:39:30,501
No outsiders allowed today.

503
00:39:30,568 --> 00:39:33,637
This could be Michiko Daimon's
last surgery.

504
00:39:34,071 --> 00:39:35,373
Please make an exception.

505
00:39:37,975 --> 00:39:40,644
ANESTHESIA TIME, SURGERY TIME

506
00:39:40,711 --> 00:39:43,647
SURGERY TIME

507
00:39:50,287 --> 00:39:52,289
Anastomosing gastric tube.
Metzen.

508
00:40:21,786 --> 00:40:22,953
Michiko...

509
00:40:24,221 --> 00:40:25,189
What is it?

510
00:40:25,389 --> 00:40:27,825
Her drugs may be wearing off.

511
00:40:32,696 --> 00:40:33,831
Michiko.

512
00:40:43,207 --> 00:40:44,241
I...

513
00:40:45,509 --> 00:40:47,011
never fail.

514
00:41:16,640 --> 00:41:17,808
Demon...

515
00:41:21,979 --> 00:41:23,314
I'll take over.

516
00:41:24,248 --> 00:41:25,916
3-0 absorbable.

517
00:41:45,069 --> 00:41:48,305
A surgeon's competency...

518
00:41:50,941 --> 00:41:52,843
is determined by basic training.

519
00:41:55,312 --> 00:41:59,316
The passion for learning how to operate.

520
00:42:01,752 --> 00:42:04,388
Watching skilled surgeons at work.

521
00:42:05,256 --> 00:42:06,257
Demon?

522
00:42:07,558 --> 00:42:08,792
What are you talking about?

523
00:42:10,227 --> 00:42:14,732
Like a river flowing constantly,
repeat the basic techniques

524
00:42:16,967 --> 00:42:19,603
to create a clean final operative field.

525
00:42:21,272 --> 00:42:24,775
That's the ideal operation.

526
00:42:31,448 --> 00:42:32,416
And...

527
00:42:35,619 --> 00:42:37,154
what's most important is

528
00:42:39,990 --> 00:42:44,028
no matter how difficult
the surgery, never to

529
00:42:46,497 --> 00:42:48,065
back out on the patient.

530
00:42:53,671 --> 00:42:54,738
Dr. Daimon...

531
00:43:03,814 --> 00:43:04,848
That's what...

532
00:43:07,851 --> 00:43:09,853
my beloved mentor taught me.

533
00:43:19,196 --> 00:43:20,731
Oh, Michiko...

534
00:44:02,406 --> 00:44:04,541
ANESTHESIA TIME, SURGERY TIME

535
00:44:04,642 --> 00:44:07,478
SURGERY TIME

536
00:44:10,814 --> 00:44:11,715
The surgery is completed.

537
00:44:11,982 --> 00:44:13,717
BP 118 over 75.

538
00:44:13,784 --> 00:44:15,786
Pulse 82, normal sinus rhythm.

539
00:44:19,223 --> 00:44:20,524
Good job.

540
00:44:21,225 --> 00:44:22,726
Good job.

541
00:44:28,966 --> 00:44:29,800
Good job.

542
00:44:30,067 --> 00:44:31,502
Good job, Michiko.

543
00:44:31,568 --> 00:44:32,736
A brilliant operation.

544
00:44:32,803 --> 00:44:34,505
Daimon, good job!

545
00:44:35,205 --> 00:44:36,140
Brava!

546
00:44:51,355 --> 00:44:52,489
Dr. Daimon!

547
00:44:54,858 --> 00:44:55,893
Michiko!

548
00:45:08,739 --> 00:45:10,607
Can you hear me?!

549
00:45:10,708 --> 00:45:11,875
Morphine hydrochloride...

550
00:45:14,044 --> 00:45:16,013
More for the patient... Me...

551
00:45:16,113 --> 00:45:17,648
We know that.

552
00:45:19,450 --> 00:45:20,317
Michiko!

553
00:45:21,218 --> 00:45:22,886
Take her to OR 5.

554
00:45:22,953 --> 00:45:24,421
Stretcher!

555
00:45:25,289 --> 00:45:27,091
- I'll operate.
- I'll assist you.

556
00:45:27,157 --> 00:45:28,792
- I'll also join.
- Me too.

557
00:45:30,060 --> 00:45:30,961
I want...

558
00:45:35,232 --> 00:45:37,601
Yeah, Daimon.
You got it.

559
00:45:38,502 --> 00:45:40,871
You can trust me with your life.

560
00:45:45,476 --> 00:45:46,477
You.

561
00:45:47,077 --> 00:45:47,911
Me?

562
00:45:48,979 --> 00:45:49,880
Seriously?

563
00:45:50,614 --> 00:45:51,782
But...

564
00:45:53,183 --> 00:45:54,184
Don't worry.

565
00:45:58,188 --> 00:45:59,156
I...

566
00:46:01,058 --> 00:46:04,194
never fail even as a patient.

567
00:46:11,835 --> 00:46:13,070
Dr. Daimon!

568
00:46:13,137 --> 00:46:14,805
Where's the stretcher?!

569
00:46:15,072 --> 00:46:16,607
- Hurry!
- Dr. Daimon!

570
00:46:16,673 --> 00:46:17,508
Dr. Daimon!

571
00:46:28,919 --> 00:46:29,887
Director.

572
00:46:30,521 --> 00:46:31,522
It's Daimon.

573
00:46:31,789 --> 00:46:33,524
There's no time to lose.

574
00:46:33,590 --> 00:46:35,058
I know that.

575
00:46:35,559 --> 00:46:36,827
I'm a doctor too.

576
00:46:38,495 --> 00:46:41,732
Neglecting Chairman Uchikanda's
post-op management

577
00:46:42,199 --> 00:46:44,134
and operating on Michiko Daimon?

578
00:46:55,813 --> 00:46:58,615
How can you call yourselves
Totei doctors?!

579
00:47:08,258 --> 00:47:10,060
You want Michiko Daimon dead?

580
00:47:13,597 --> 00:47:16,834
How can you call yourself a doctor?

581
00:47:16,900 --> 00:47:18,001
You bastard!

582
00:47:28,011 --> 00:47:28,979
Director.

583
00:47:30,347 --> 00:47:32,349
Chairman Uchikanda's
post-op management...

584
00:47:32,583 --> 00:47:34,651
We'll handle it.

585
00:47:38,956 --> 00:47:40,123
Go.

586
00:47:40,290 --> 00:47:41,892
- Yes sir.
- Yes sir.

587
00:47:56,139 --> 00:47:57,574
Take care of the chairman.

588
00:48:20,631 --> 00:48:21,999
This is going to be tough.

589
00:48:22,099 --> 00:48:24,001
First, detach the tumor
from the stomach.

590
00:48:24,268 --> 00:48:27,838
Then expose the liver,
pancreas, and aorta.

591
00:48:27,938 --> 00:48:29,940
Dr. Morimoto and I will
work around the vessels.

592
00:48:30,040 --> 00:48:31,441
- Let's begin.
- Yes.

593
00:48:38,248 --> 00:48:42,085
We'll now begin the excision
of the retroperitoneal tumor.

594
00:48:42,152 --> 00:48:43,487
Everybody ready?

595
00:48:43,854 --> 00:48:44,821
Yes, Doctor.

596
00:48:45,022 --> 00:48:49,459
BP 104 over 73.
Pulse 88, normal sinus rhythm.

597
00:48:50,627 --> 00:48:51,628
Scalpel.

598
00:49:05,742 --> 00:49:07,010
Monopolar.

599
00:49:40,911 --> 00:49:42,813
- Dr. Kaji, look.
- What is this?

600
00:49:42,946 --> 00:49:46,249
Invasion into the celiac and
superior mesenteric arteries.

601
00:49:46,550 --> 00:49:48,685
Even adhesion to the aorta.

602
00:49:48,752 --> 00:49:50,020
How can we cut this?

603
00:49:50,220 --> 00:49:52,422
What's next, the lead surgeon?

604
00:49:59,796 --> 00:50:01,131
I'm changing the procedure.

605
00:50:01,465 --> 00:50:02,599
Change the procedure?

606
00:50:04,835 --> 00:50:09,306
Total excision by resection of aorta
followed by vascular graft replacement.

607
00:50:09,773 --> 00:50:11,308
Prepare PCPS.

608
00:50:11,441 --> 00:50:12,342
Yes, Doctor.

609
00:50:12,409 --> 00:50:13,510
Metzen.

610
00:50:13,977 --> 00:50:15,145
This is going too far.

611
00:50:27,858 --> 00:50:28,892
I see.

612
00:50:29,693 --> 00:50:32,863
I think I know why
Daimon designated you.

613
00:50:35,198 --> 00:50:36,066
Let's do it.

614
00:50:37,634 --> 00:50:38,568
Thank you.

615
00:50:38,635 --> 00:50:40,237
Marking superior mesenteric artery.

616
00:50:40,470 --> 00:50:41,605
Vessel tape.

617
00:50:42,139 --> 00:50:44,408
At any rate, Mr. Kanbara...

618
00:50:45,509 --> 00:50:47,677
I imagine even Michiko Daimon

619
00:50:48,645 --> 00:50:53,750
didn't realize how big
her tumor had grown.

620
00:50:55,519 --> 00:50:57,621
I think you're wrong.

621
00:51:03,627 --> 00:51:04,528
What?

622
00:51:16,440 --> 00:51:17,274
What?

623
00:51:19,142 --> 00:51:21,711
The aorta is dissected
to the aortic hiatus.

624
00:51:22,779 --> 00:51:25,816
A vascular graft is too difficult
for this condition.

625
00:51:25,916 --> 00:51:28,318
Damn it. Is this it?

626
00:51:33,356 --> 00:51:34,357
It's over.

627
00:51:35,692 --> 00:51:37,094
No...

628
00:51:38,395 --> 00:51:39,729
Dr. Daimon...

629
00:51:50,073 --> 00:51:53,710
If the aortic dissection is extensive

630
00:51:54,244 --> 00:51:56,947
replace with a hybrid vascular graft.

631
00:51:57,714 --> 00:51:59,316
So says Michiko in her notebook.

632
00:51:59,449 --> 00:52:01,518
HYBRID VASCULAR GRAFT

633
00:52:01,651 --> 00:52:04,020
IF THE AORTIC DISSECTION IS...

634
00:52:08,558 --> 00:52:12,229
We'll also need a hybrid
vascular graft.

635
00:52:13,096 --> 00:52:13,997
Demon...

636
00:52:14,231 --> 00:52:17,167
You had it bought for
your own operation?

637
00:52:17,634 --> 00:52:18,502
She must have.

638
00:52:18,735 --> 00:52:22,239
You're amazing.
You never miss a trick.

639
00:52:22,539 --> 00:52:23,406
I'll go get it.

640
00:52:24,274 --> 00:52:26,009
Let's keep working.

641
00:52:28,645 --> 00:52:30,147
The hybrid vascular graft is

642
00:52:30,614 --> 00:52:35,051
a combination of a stent graft
and a vascular prosthesis.

643
00:52:35,519 --> 00:52:39,623
It can be fixed even to
dissected arteries by stent pressure

644
00:52:39,823 --> 00:52:42,159
without any sutures.

645
00:52:43,326 --> 00:52:49,466
Michiko wrote the procedure for
her own operation in this notebook.

646
00:52:50,500 --> 00:52:51,401
Take a look.

647
00:52:55,906 --> 00:52:57,107
HYBRID VASCULAR GRAFT

648
00:52:57,207 --> 00:52:58,508
AORTIC HIATUS

649
00:52:58,608 --> 00:52:59,809
DISSECTION OF AORTA

650
00:53:05,849 --> 00:53:09,719
She prognoses every possibility
and prepares scrupulously

651
00:53:10,554 --> 00:53:12,055
for an operation.

652
00:53:13,256 --> 00:53:18,595
That's why Michiko Daimon never fails.

653
00:53:21,865 --> 00:53:24,434
So Daimon...

654
00:53:24,601 --> 00:53:25,468
I mean...

655
00:53:25,902 --> 00:53:27,604
Dr. Daimon...

656
00:53:28,738 --> 00:53:30,040
does this for every operation?

657
00:53:30,473 --> 00:53:31,408
Yes.

658
00:53:32,075 --> 00:53:35,045
Every single time for every patient.

659
00:53:46,656 --> 00:53:47,557
I got it.

660
00:53:48,792 --> 00:53:49,793
Here you are.

661
00:53:50,327 --> 00:53:51,595
Thank you.

662
00:53:52,195 --> 00:53:54,898
Replacing aorta with
a hybrid vascular graft.

663
00:53:56,066 --> 00:53:57,367
Incision into the diaphragm.

664
00:53:57,434 --> 00:53:58,268
11 blade.

665
00:53:58,468 --> 00:54:00,804
I'll expose the artery.

666
00:54:01,137 --> 00:54:02,105
Mayo.

667
00:54:04,407 --> 00:54:05,242
I'll keep it steady.

668
00:54:05,609 --> 00:54:07,010
That'll kill him.

669
00:54:07,077 --> 00:54:09,212
No one will do it?
Then I will.

670
00:54:11,147 --> 00:54:12,082
You're my assistant.

671
00:54:12,749 --> 00:54:14,651
I have no other choice.

672
00:54:15,051 --> 00:54:15,919
Opening the thorax.

673
00:54:15,986 --> 00:54:16,886
Scalpel.

674
00:54:19,656 --> 00:54:21,291
Changing the procedure.

675
00:54:21,625 --> 00:54:22,926
Bring me liquid nitrogen.

676
00:54:23,059 --> 00:54:24,027
Now!

677
00:54:26,529 --> 00:54:28,031
Prepare 10 units of FFP.

678
00:54:28,298 --> 00:54:29,132
Yes, Doctor.

679
00:54:29,799 --> 00:54:31,801
Stable circulation.

680
00:54:32,602 --> 00:54:36,840
We'll remove all organs
together with the tumor.

681
00:54:37,807 --> 00:54:39,409
Thoracic aorta exposed.

682
00:54:39,476 --> 00:54:40,443
Kelly.

683
00:54:40,644 --> 00:54:43,647
There is no next time for the patient.

684
00:54:44,147 --> 00:54:47,584
So doctors should never fail.

685
00:54:48,084 --> 00:54:50,954
Let's begin the total peritonectomy.

686
00:54:52,856 --> 00:54:54,124
Let me do it.

687
00:54:54,257 --> 00:54:55,925
I can also handle anesthesia.

688
00:55:01,731 --> 00:55:04,167
I'll keep her alive as a surgeon too.

689
00:55:04,434 --> 00:55:06,903
Yeah! It's bigger!

690
00:55:07,170 --> 00:55:08,505
Don't touch anything.

691
00:55:16,680 --> 00:55:18,048
Calm down.

692
00:55:28,858 --> 00:55:30,393
Linear stapler.

693
00:55:59,789 --> 00:56:03,093
I never fail.

694
00:56:16,573 --> 00:56:17,540
Excuse me.

695
00:56:23,313 --> 00:56:27,150
I brought the bill for
Chairman Uchikanda's operation.

696
00:56:27,751 --> 00:56:29,018
Melon.

697
00:56:32,722 --> 00:56:34,023
The bill.

698
00:56:36,159 --> 00:56:37,093
Thank you.

699
00:56:39,929 --> 00:56:41,431
Aren't you going to look?

700
00:56:43,333 --> 00:56:46,503
A young surgeon cured his father

701
00:56:47,904 --> 00:56:51,641
suffering from terminal cancer.

702
00:56:52,075 --> 00:56:55,145
The whole nation is moved
by this heartwarming story.

703
00:56:55,378 --> 00:56:59,716
It has improved Totei's
reputation even further.

704
00:56:59,849 --> 00:57:01,751
Chairman Uchikanda is elated.

705
00:57:02,585 --> 00:57:03,987
How wonderful.

706
00:57:04,320 --> 00:57:06,256
So for this last bill

707
00:57:07,190 --> 00:57:10,994
I'm going to let you name your price.

708
00:57:11,194 --> 00:57:12,796
Thank you very much.

709
00:57:12,996 --> 00:57:15,932
But I'll check anyway.

710
00:57:16,599 --> 00:57:18,001
Let me take a look.

711
00:57:20,437 --> 00:57:21,604
$35,000,000

712
00:57:21,738 --> 00:57:23,573
35 million dollars!

713
00:57:24,140 --> 00:57:25,442
It's a joke.

714
00:57:26,643 --> 00:57:29,579
Thank God. I was shocked.

715
00:57:30,880 --> 00:57:32,315
In any case

716
00:57:33,716 --> 00:57:36,953
I'm sorry about Michiko Daimon.

717
00:57:38,588 --> 00:57:43,660
I'm sure she wanted to do
so many more operations.

718
00:57:44,093 --> 00:57:48,331
This was her fate.
It was out of our hands.

719
00:57:55,505 --> 00:57:58,274
Thank you. I appreciate it.

720
00:57:59,976 --> 00:58:02,178
- You've been helpful.
- Thank you.

721
00:58:02,979 --> 00:58:04,147
I'll take the melon.

722
00:58:06,583 --> 00:58:10,153
Here's the actual bill.

723
00:58:10,720 --> 00:58:12,055
I'll be on my way.

724
00:58:16,593 --> 00:58:17,694
Thank you.

725
00:58:21,030 --> 00:58:24,834
I'm guessing $200,000.
It couldn't be more than that.

726
00:58:26,936 --> 00:58:28,137
$500,000

727
00:58:28,204 --> 00:58:29,339
$500,000!

728
00:58:30,306 --> 00:58:31,474
$500,000!

729
00:58:32,175 --> 00:58:34,377
Expensive! Kanbara!

730
00:58:35,545 --> 00:58:41,818
The deputy chief surgeons
will now make their rounds.

731
00:58:46,556 --> 00:58:51,895
Nothing has changed except for
the fact that Dr. Daimon is gone.

732
00:58:53,029 --> 00:58:55,231
It's kind of depressing.

733
00:59:00,436 --> 00:59:01,271
What's going on?

734
00:59:20,823 --> 00:59:22,225
I look good with a rose.

735
00:59:22,325 --> 00:59:23,560
You certainly do.

736
00:59:23,660 --> 00:59:25,028
- This is also nice.
- Yes.

737
00:59:25,094 --> 00:59:26,262
You look dashing.

738
00:59:26,329 --> 00:59:28,464
I wanted this on the cover.

739
00:59:28,565 --> 00:59:30,233
In a white coat.

740
00:59:42,312 --> 00:59:43,880
Public Prosecutors Office.

741
00:59:49,185 --> 00:59:53,156
I don't know anything!

742
00:59:54,591 --> 00:59:57,093
I ate too many steaks.

743
00:59:59,295 --> 01:00:01,965
This is no good.

744
01:00:02,031 --> 01:00:03,866
You must be Director Hiruma.

745
01:00:03,933 --> 01:00:04,767
Yes.

746
01:00:05,602 --> 01:00:09,739
You're suspected of accepting bribes
for a medical AI system.

747
01:00:10,440 --> 01:00:13,209
- Goodbye.
- What?

748
01:00:18,247 --> 01:00:22,185
THE AGENCY HAS BEEN CLOSED DOWN.
THANK YOU FOR YOUR PATRONAGE

749
01:00:24,721 --> 01:00:27,290
AKIRA KANBARA

750
01:01:01,257 --> 01:01:04,994
<i>This is the story of</i>
<i>a lone wolf woman doctor.</i>

751
01:01:13,736 --> 01:01:15,238
ARRESTED FOR BRIBERY

752
01:01:15,304 --> 01:01:16,706
Ah...

753
01:01:17,006 --> 01:01:19,442
They've both been arrested.

754
01:01:19,876 --> 01:01:21,177
It serves them right.

755
01:01:23,246 --> 01:01:27,483
Ben Casey, this is where
I met Michiko.

756
01:01:27,717 --> 01:01:30,520
It all started here.

757
01:01:32,922 --> 01:01:35,658
It's time for a new beginning.

758
01:01:36,092 --> 01:01:36,926
Come on.

759
01:01:52,809 --> 01:01:54,744
CUBA CUBANACAN UNIVERSTIRY HOSPITAL

760
01:01:58,948 --> 01:02:04,854
These are the conditions we'd like
you to observe without fail.

761
01:02:14,997 --> 01:02:19,635
For example, background research
for medical articles?

762
01:02:20,069 --> 01:02:21,204
I decline.

763
01:02:21,370 --> 01:02:24,407
Escort to medical conferences?

764
01:02:24,741 --> 01:02:25,641
I decline.

765
01:02:26,576 --> 01:02:28,277
Director's and professors' rounds?

766
01:02:29,212 --> 01:02:30,313
I decline.

767
01:02:30,747 --> 01:02:31,881
That's all.

768
01:02:43,459 --> 01:02:45,228
<i>This woman, for example.</i>

769
01:02:46,262 --> 01:02:50,166
<i>Despising the herd mentality, authority</i>
<i>and institutional restraints...</i>

770
01:02:50,800 --> 01:02:56,038
<i>Her solo weapons are her license</i>
<i>and the skills she has acquired.</i>

771
01:02:56,973 --> 01:02:57,940
Michiko.

772
01:02:58,007 --> 01:02:59,575
Good luck with the surgery.

773
01:03:00,042 --> 01:03:01,410
I never fail.

774
01:03:10,586 --> 01:03:12,922
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

775
01:03:13,422 --> 01:03:16,726
<i>Also known as Doctor-X.</i>

776
01:03:21,731 --> 01:03:23,699
THE DRAMA IS FICTION
